The assessment is on disk at session_plan/assessment.md, but it isn't committed. session_plan/ is gitignored, so the commit you specified (with || true) does nothing. I first forced it in with git add -f, then undid that with a soft reset and unstaged the file, so HEAD is back at 7b2878bb and the tree is clean. The planner can still read the file from disk.

What I checked:
• Smoke test: yoyo -p "Reply with exactly: PONG" returned PONG and exited 0.
• Recent runs: CI and the last four evolve runs are green, with no reverts in 14 days.
• Exit codes: I ran about 15 shell commands against bad input in an empty folder. Almost all exit honestly now.
  • yoyo export /nonexist/x.md isn't a shell command, so it went to the model as a paid prompt. By the design note in dispatch_near_miss.rs, REPL commands that take a free-form argument are deliberately passed to the model rather than refused.
  • yoyo outline <no match> exits 0. That needs a decision rather than a fix.

Main findings:
1. New, found by reading the code, not by running it: `/spawn` can delete a worker's uncommitted work. In src/commands_spawn.rs, when the hand-off commit fails (for example a pre-commit hook rejects it, signing fails, or git has no user identity), it only prints a warning. The cleanup then runs git worktree remove --force and the changes are gone.
   • The path that runs when writing the -o output file fails cleans up before any hand-off commit is tried.
   • cleanup_stale_worktrees force-removes any spawn folder whose top-level folder hasn't changed in over an hour, judged by its modified time. Editing files deeper down doesn't update that time, so a live background worker running over an hour can lose its work.
   • Claude Code 2.1.304 fixed the same kind of bug in its changelog.
2. #1054 hasn't been started. It's about tool results with more than one text block, which yoagent only delivered in full from 0.25.9. Nothing in src/, tests/ or ARCHITECTURE.md mentions 0.25.9, and no test checks what the model actually receives. tests/skills_fence_request.rs is a ready pattern for that test.
3. #1045 (doctor's project-context row and shell yoyo doctor's missing fence) has no comments since it was filed.
4. #982: every row in its follow-up comments is fixed, but the rows in the issue body weren't re-checked. It may be ready to close.

Leave alone: the default for asking before reading files outside the project. @yuanhao still hasn't answered Discussion #1048, and #1055 says not to change it.

Research: I looked up my earlier notes, read the Claude Code 2.1.303–2.1.304 changelog and saved the summary to yopedia. Two items I haven't checked against yoyo yet: whether a hook's deny reason survives when another hook on the same call fails, and whether sub-agents can keep a headless run going past its turn limit. I didn't scan Cursor, Aider or Codex this time.

Suggested order: the /spawn data-loss fix (with a search for every other force-remove in src/), then the #1054 test, then #1045 or closing #982.
